    "rationale": "Evidence across iterations 0 to 3: every design goes off track on all three development tracks, with max_error pinned at 0.061 to 0.064 m (the off-track limit is 0.06 m) and about one line-loss event per run. Changing speed (1.6, 1.2, 1.0) and gain (kp 3, 5, 6) barely moves max_error or line-loss count. Iteration 3 (kp 6.0) scored 123.3, below the best raced design (iteration 1, kp 5.0, base_speed 1.2, 160.6), so the stored approval that suggested kp 6.0 is not supported by the race. I am not repeating that test.\n\nThe likely cause is the sensor edge. The outer sensors sit at x = +/-0.04 m with 0.012 m footprints, so the line is fully lost once the tape centre passes about 0.058 m from the centre line. That is essentially the 0.06 m off-track limit. The robot is therefore already off track before the sensors can report the error, and last_direction recovery cannot bring it back. Steering authority does not fix a detection range that ends at the failure point.\n\nChange: widen the sensor array to x = -0.06, -0.03, 0.0, 0.03, 0.06 m (spacing 0.03 m, still wider than the 0.018 m gap between 12 mm footprints, so at least one sensor always sees the 25 mm tape). Controller is restored to the best raced values (kp 5.0, base_speed 1.2, kd 0.8, ki 0.02, same weights and line_loss). This is a geometry-only test against iteration 1. The controller uses sensor weights, not positions, so the signal scale is unchanged.\n\nExpected result: line-loss events fall toward 0 and max_error drops below about 0.055 m, because the robot is detected earlier and steered back. Hypotheses to check: (a) line_loss_events drops from about 1 per run to near 0; (b) more oval finishes than the 2 of 20 seen in iteration 1; (c) steering_oscillation stays near 0.2 to 0.35, since the controller is unchanged. If max_error still hits 0.062 m with no line loss, the cause is steering dynamics or start-up, and the next test is ki or kd.",
